  THE FEATURE-10 AUDIT -- every paired contrast, re-read with voicing and
  loudness DROPPED from the features (`m3_timbre_features`, 7 groups).
  `echo` cannot distinguish a real effect from one feature being driven
  toward zero variance and amplified by the sd floor; `artic` can.
    contrast            d echo             d ARTIC
    taught - none   +0.0108 +- 0.0053  +0.0094 +- 0.0066  (2.1 SE vs 1.4 SE)
    yoked  - none   +0.0072 +- 0.0058  +0.0154 +- 0.0073  (1.2 SE vs 2.1 SE)
    taught - yoked  +0.0036 +- 0.0051  -0.0059 +- 0.0064  (0.7 SE vs 0.9 SE)

  THE AUDIT IS INCONCLUSIVE. `yoked - none` is +0.0154 +- 0.0073
  (2.1 SE) on the articulator features: the same sign but under the
  3 SE bar. The published +0.0673 is then PARTLY feature 10 by an
  amount this n cannot resolve, and it should be quoted with this
  column beside it rather than alone.

  SECONDARY, paired taught - none echo   +0.0108 +- 0.0053  (2.1 SE, n=36)
  the power          at this n the smallest resolvable change is 0.0105
                     (2 SE), which is 3% of the taught arm's margin
                     over chance. A null here BOUNDS what the lesson
                     costs the echo; it does not show it costs nothing.

  THE DISCRIMINATOR -- is the taught arm's excess the naming response?
    yoked echo                   0.898+-0.004   (none 0.891, taught 0.902)
    paired taught - yoked        +0.0036 +- 0.0051 (0.7 SE, n=36)
    yoked naming over its null   +0.0062    (taught +0.0108)
    its scored trials            200 of 200 (taught 200, none 200)

  WHAT LIVING A SESSION COSTS, paired none - fresh   +0.0026 +- 0.0061 (0.4 SE)

  PRIMARY, both on the SAME 36 creatures
    (a) echo on the taught arm   0.902  against the 0.75 bar      MET
    (b) naming above its null    +0.0108 +- 0.0199 (0.5 SE)   NOT MET

  NOT MET, and the 4th rung is why: naming reads +0.0108 over its own
  null at 0.5 SE, under the 3 SE bar. The echo number above is then
  not evidence of composition -- a surviving echo on a creature that
  learned nothing is just the untaught property, measured twice.
